    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0280" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115 Eastern States Petroleum Co./79:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Malaga</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Callanan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Malaga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-10T12:00:00+00:00">February 10,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Your No. 3, February 8, 7 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d247-f1"/> Captain Lewis
                    arrived here this morning and has resumed charge of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nantucket Chief</hi>. Port captain in reply to my inquiry stated at 11:30
                    that his instructions were to hand over the ship to Captain Lewis through the
                    intermediary of the Consulate which he will not be able to do until 4:30 p.m.
                    today, although I requested that the matter be [expedited?].<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d247-f2"/> Ambassador not informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Callanan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d247-f1" n="28" xml:id="d247-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d247-f2" n="29" xml:id="d247-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram of February 10, 6 p.m., the Consul at Gibraltar informed the
                    Department that the <hi rendition="#italic">Nantucket Chief</hi> had sailed for
                    Gibraltar at 6 p.m. (352.115 Eastern States Petroleum Co./80).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
